Preserve variable-frame-rate decode timestamps with VideoToolbox reordering.

The upstream reorder-depth correction (0057) fixes constant-rate H.264, but
subtracting the initial time offset from every VideoToolbox DTS is still wrong
when later input frame intervals grow. Delay the submitted presentation timeline
by the encoder's reorder depth instead, using a FIFO of pending timestamps plus
the reorder window.
Only the initial decode prefix is extrapolated; presentation timestamps and
compressed packets remain unchanged. Short clips without a complete reorder
window use their submitted timestamps directly. Release the FIFO on every close,
including failed initialization and cancellation.

Covered by snow-recording-export/tests/videotoolbox_timing.rs for both H.264 and
HEVC, including the increasing gaps that fail with only the upstream backport.

